BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chess and Culture: Learn to Play Chess
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T130000
UID:chess-and-culture-learn-to-play-chess-2026-08-15t13-00-00-04-00@agakha
 nmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/07
 /DSC_4476-1-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gra
 vity
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an afternoon of strategy\, discovery\, and play at
  the Aga Khan Museum.\n\nBegin with a guided tour of the Museum’s galler
 ies\, where you’ll explore stories\, objects\, and artistic traditions f
 rom diverse cultures and civilizations. Then\, learn the basics of chess w
 ith instructors from the Chess Institute of Canada. This interactive works
 hop will introduce the rules and strategies of the game\, followed by frie
 ndly matches to practice your new skills.\n\nThis workshop is suitable for
  all skill levels and ages. No prior experience is required.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/chess-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ali Sethi’s ‘Harmonium: A Roots Residency'
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T200000
UID:ali-sethi-s-harmonium-a-roots-residency-2026-08-28t20-00-00-04-00@agak
 hanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Ali-Sethi-Website-Image-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled-1.jpg?resize
 =1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a mesmerizing performance blending South Asian mel
 odies with global beats\, and drawing on “folk” and “woke” iconogr
 aphies to tell powerful tales of identity.\n\nWhat are my roots\, asks mus
 ician Ali Sethi\, in this playful\, shape-shifting concert built around th
 e sound of his beloved harmonium. Ghazals\, qawwalis\, and avant-garde pop
  songs all merge and diverge as they tell a fascinating story about the sy
 ncretic nature of South Asian culture in the present day.\n\nMeet and Gree
 t • 6:30–7 pm
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/ali-sethi/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
